.TH "YAMLR-FMT" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBCanonical Kubernetes Manifest Formatter (k8sfmt / yamlfix)\fR
.PP
The \fBfmt\fR command canonicalizes the layout of Kubernetes manifests according to the official Kubernetes OpenAPI schema hierarchy, emulating the authority of \fBgofmt\fR for Kubernetes manifests.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
yamlr fmt [PATH] [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Formats manifest key ordering and indentation deterministically:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Canonical Ordering**: Reorders root keys to the authoritative Kubernetes hierarchy:
    \fBapiVersion\fR -> \fBkind\fR -> \fBmetadata\fR -> \fBspec\fR -> \fBdata\fR -> \fBstatus\fR.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Comment & Blank-Line Preservation**: Preserves all inline and block comments, whitespace, and formatting.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Multi-Document & CRLF Preservation**: Preserves \fB---\fR document boundaries and handles Windows (\fB\r\n\fR) and Unix (\fB\n\fR) line endings without corruption.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Pre-Write Schema Gate**: When writing in-place (\fB-w\fR), every file is audited against official Kubernetes OpenAPI schemas (\fBverify_no_schema_regression\fR) to guarantee formatting never introduces structural corruption.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Atomic Write & Backup**: In-place writes use atomic temporary-file swaps and generate \fB.bak\fR backups to prevent half-written or corrupted files on crash.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **POSIX Pipe Streaming**: Supports stdin/stdout streaming via \fB-\fR:
.nf
.RS
    cat deployment.yaml | yamlr fmt - | kubectl apply -f -
    helm template my-chart | yamlr fmt - | gitops-sync
.RE
.fi
.SH "FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB-w, --write\fR: Write formatted output back to source files in-place with atomic backup and schema gating (default prints to stdout).
The target path defaults to \fB.\fR. Use \fB-\fR to read from stdin. Unknown options and multiple target paths are rejected. Read, traversal, and write failures return a nonzero system-error status.
.PP
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
# Preview formatting of all manifests in the current directory
yamlr fmt .

# Format and rewrite manifests in-place with schema gate verification
yamlr fmt -w ./k8s

# Format a single manifest streamed through a Unix pipeline
helm template my-chart | yamlr fmt -
.RE
.fi
